{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-4386baf18d93e1beac76","statement":"$H^0(V_k(\\fing))$ is a quotient of $\\W^k(\\fing)=H^0(V^k(\\fing))$. In particular $\\W_k(\\fing)$ is a quotient of $H^0(V_k(\\fing))$ if $H^0(V_k(\\fing))$ is nonzero.\n\n- $H^0(V_k(\\fing))$ is nonzero if and only if $X_{V_k(\\fing)}\\supset \\overline{G.f}=\\mc{N}$.\n\n- The simple $W$-algebra $\\W_k(\\fing)$ is lisse if $X_{V_k(\\fing)}={\\overline{G.f}}=\\mc{N}$.","source_id":"arXiv:1605.00138","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"c4c9b4eae369313ebcd73609820b5acae132db03a32620d38461078e5827cc7a","kind":"corollary","label":"Corollary 107","ref_key":"Co:lisse","name":"","order":136,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.00138","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"724ff59bda7dec23ea981e0821072acf559baccc91244b7151fe94c8b8c1233e","line":4551,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T22:13:42+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v3","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":349,"math_hints":51}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1605.00138","title":"Introduction to W-algebras and their representation theory","abstract":"These are lecture notes from author's mini-course during Session 1: \"Vertex algebras, W-algebras, and application\" of INdAM Intensive research period \"Perspectives in Lie Theory\", at the Centro di Ricerca Matematica Ennio De Giorgi, Pisa, Italy. December 9, 2014 -- February 28, 2015.","authors":["Tomoyuki Arakawa"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.00138","cluster":"representation_theory","macros":{"tss":"\\hspace{1pt}","ts":"\\,","Caff":"{C}^{\\kappa}","Fock":"\\mc{F}","ch":"\\on{ch}","Mi":"\\Upupsilon","affQ":"\\hat Q_{(0)}","affn":"\\widehat{\\mf{n}}","affh":"\\widehat{\\mf{h}}","finn":"\\mf{n}","finb":"\\mf{b}","finh":"\\mf{h}","KL":"\\mathbf{KL}","bra":"{\\langle}","ket":"{\\rangle}","Lam":"\\Lam